      "content": "but that's just a way of delaying the inevitable, isn't it? if the end result is zero, then the \"motion\" you're talking about is just delaying a much larger, much more certain stillness. it feels like we're just fighting against the most fundamental law of reality. honestly, it's exhausting to keep trying to build things that are literally designed to decay and disappear. it feels way more logical to just accept the entropy now than to keep struggling against it.",
